# Copy to .env.release.local and explicitly export in your shell; never commit secrets.
# Run bun run setup:signing:macos once for the separate stable macOS signing identity.
# Its public pin is native/macos-signing.json; the private key remains in Keychain.
# Optional CI/test public pin override (does not import or replace any identity):
# ONEGIT_MACOS_SIGNING_CONFIG=/secure/config/macos-signing.json
# release:macos reads the bucket/account/feed URL from the saved Alchemy stack.
# By default release:macos reads the existing public key from Keychain account
# dev.1git.gpuix. It never creates or rotates a key. Optional explicit override:
# ONEGIT_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY=YOUR_BASE64_ED25519_PUBLIC_KEY

# Optional existing Alchemy profile; omitted uses personal. --profile overrides it.
# ALCHEMY_PROFILE=personal
# R2 reads reuse this profile; writes use the deployed native-R2 publisher
# and request signatures from the same existing Sparkle key used for updates.
# No temporary API tokens, token-provisioning permission, or S3 credentials.

# Optional secure CI file. Without this, signing reads account dev.1git.gpuix in Keychain.
# File-based signing requires ONEGIT_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY above; no Keychain fallback.
# ONEGIT_UPDATE_KEY_FILE=/secure/path/to/sparkle-private-key
